---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { grantOfferById } from '../../lib/grants';
import templateText from '../../../public/downloads/grant-letter-of-inquiry-template.txt?raw';

const pageTitle = 'Grant Letter of Inquiry Example & Free Template';
const pageDescription = 'Read a fictional nonprofit grant letter of inquiry example, then copy or download a free LOI template with prompts for your request, program and budget.';

const siteOrigin = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://www.wellridgegroup.com');
const siteURL = siteOrigin.toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const sampleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: pageTitle,
  description: pageDescription,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wellridge Group' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wellridge Group', url: siteURL },
  mainEntityOfPage: `${siteURL}/work-examples/letter-of-inquiry`,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} structuredData={sampleSchema}>
  <article class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ridge-blue">Work example · fictional demonstration</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-3 mb-6">Grant letter of inquiry example and free template</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6">Wellridge Group · September 9, 2026</p>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 mb-6">A grant letter of inquiry introduces your organization, proposed work and funding request so a foundation can consider fit and the next step. Use the blank structure below, then see how a fictional nonprofit presents its program, budget and planning targets.</p>
      <nav aria-label="On this page" class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-8"><a href="#loi-template" class="text-ridge-blue underline font-medium">Copy the free template</a><a href="#fictional-example" class="text-ridge-blue underline font-medium">Read the fictional example</a></nav>
      <div class="bg-slate-deep text-white rounded-lg p-6 text-lg"><strong>Important:</strong> Northside Arts Workshop and the Evergreen Community Arts Fund are fictional. This page is a writing demonstration, not a real client, funder, request, award, endorsement, or achieved result.</div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-gray-700">Sample premise: imagine Northside Arts Workshop is asking a local arts funder whether it would invite a short application for one existing, approved workshop plan. The facts below carry forward the fictional grant-review example; the funder name, contact details, inquiry framing, and signatory name and role are invented for this sample.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section id="loi-template" class="py-16 bg-white scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="template-heading">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 id="template-heading" class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">A grant LOI template you can adapt</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li>Check whether the foundation accepts inquiries from your organization. Its questions, length limit and submission process take priority over this template.</li>
        <li>Copy or download the template and edit it in your own document. Replace each bracketed prompt with approved facts; remove instructions before submitting.</li>
        <li>Check that the request, total project budget and other support reconcile. Keep planned outcomes separate from achieved results, and pending funding separate from secured support.</li>
      </ol>
      <p id="template-help" class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Free to copy and adapt. No email required. The box below is a read-only template; write your organization's draft in your own document.</p>
      <label for="loi-template-text" class="block font-semibold text-slate-deep mb-2">Blank letter of inquiry template</label>
      <textarea id="loi-template-text" readonly rows="18" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="template-help" class="block w-full min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-fog p-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-deep focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ridge-blue">{templateText}</textarea>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 mt-5">
        <button id="copy-loi-template" type="button" hidden class="rounded-md bg-ridge-blue px-5 py-3 text-white font-medium focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ridge-blue focus:ring-offset-2">Copy template</button>
        <a href="/downloads/grant-letter-of-inquiry-template.txt" download="wellridge-grant-loi-template.txt" class="rounded-md border border-ridge-blue px-5 py-3 text-ridge-blue font-medium">Download template (.txt)</a>
      </div>
      <p id="template-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" class="mt-3 min-h-6 text-sm text-gray-700"></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">You can also select the text and copy it manually. The download opens in a text editor and can be pasted into Word or Google Docs.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep">Want help turning your approved plan into an LOI?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-700">Our {grantOfferById.loi.price} service covers one letter up to two pages for one identified funder, using your approved program and budget, with one revision.</p>
        <a href="/letter-of-inquiry-writing" class="inline-block mt-4 text-ridge-blue underline font-medium">See the {grantOfferById.loi.price} LOI writing service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="fictional-example" class="py-16 bg-fog scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 id="example-heading" class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">Fictional example: Northside Arts Workshop</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">The letter below demonstrates structure and clear distinctions between requested money, planned support and future targets. The organizations, people and scenario are invented; this is not a submission-ready letter.</p>
      <div class="border border-gray-200 bg-white rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-8">September 9, 2026</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Evergreen Community Arts Fund<br />Attn: Grants Team<br />Arlington, Texas</p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-gray-700">Dear Evergreen Community Arts Fund Grants Team:</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-gray-700">Northside Arts Workshop respectfully inquires whether the Evergreen Community Arts Fund would invite a short application for a free six-week visual-arts workshop in Arlington, Texas. The workshop is planned for 24 students ages 10–14, with no prior art experience required. Six Saturday sessions are planned for October 17, 24, and 31 and November 7, 14, and 21, 2026, from 10:00–11:30 a.m. Each student would receive materials, and the sessions are designed as one workshop sequence.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-gray-700">Northside is seeking $3,600 toward a $4,800 project budget: teaching artist $1,800, materials $960, space $900, transportation assistance $600, and evaluation/administration $540. Planned other support is $1,200 and is not committed or secured. The request would support delivery of the existing workshop plan, rather than a new program design.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-gray-700">The planning targets are for at least 18 of 24 enrolled students to attend five of six sessions and for at least 18 students to report at least a one-point increase on a five-point creative-confidence question from the first to final session. Sign-ins and the first-to-final confidence question would be reviewed after the workshop. Any missing follow-up would be reported explicitly. These are planning targets, not results.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-gray-700">Would the fund be willing to advise whether this project fits its current priorities and, if so, whether Northside should submit a short application? We can provide the approved program description, budget detail, and requested attachments through the fund’s stated process.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-gray-700">Thank you for considering this inquiry. We would welcome the fund’s direction on fit and next steps.</p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-gray-700">Sincerely,<br />Jordan Lee<br />Program Director<br />Northside Arts Workshop</p>
      </div>
      <a class="inline-block mt-8 px-5 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md font-medium" href="/contact?service=grant-writing&package=loi">Discuss a {grantOfferById.loi.price} LOI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">What remains unresolved before a real submission</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700"><li>Confirm the real funder’s eligibility, priorities, instructions, deadline, and required contact or portal.</li><li>Confirm Northside’s approved program, venue, accessibility, safeguarding, transportation, and budget authority.</li><li>Confirm whether the $1,200 other support is committed, planned, or removed from the request story.</li><li>Assign the accountable reviewer and final submitter; confirm required attachments and current versions.</li></ul>
      <p class="mt-8 text-gray-700">This sample pairs with the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/resources/grant-review-loi-or-application">grant review, LOI, or application guide</a>, the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/work-examples/grant-review">fictional grant review example</a>, and <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/letter-of-inquiry-writing">letter-of-inquiry writing service</a>.</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-600">For another perspective on structure and funder fit, see <a href="https://www.mtu.edu/foundations/grant-writing-guide/letter-of-inquiry/" class="text-ridge-blue underline">Michigan Tech's letter-of-inquiry guide</a>. Your actual funder's current instructions govern your submission.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const template = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#loi-template-text');
  const copyButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-loi-template');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLParagraphElement>('#template-copy-status');

  if (template && copyButton && status) {
    copyButton.hidden = false;
    copyButton.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      copyButton.disabled = true;
      status.textContent = '';
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(template.value);
        status.textContent = 'Template copied. Paste it into your document and replace the bracketed prompts.';
      } catch {
        template.focus();
        template.select();
        status.textContent = 'Automatic copy is unavailable. The template is selected; use your copy command or download the text file.';
      } finally {
        copyButton.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  }
</script>
